I've started the tools agent (Fable, own worktree). It builds `agent/site_tools.py` with:
- `search(field, query)`: fill, submit and collect every hit in one call;
- `collect(list)`: page through a list the model chose until the end;
- `extract(fields)`: one structured model call returning values with their source quotes, still grounded;
- deterministic parsers for numbers and dates, returning both readings when the day/month order is ambiguous.

The model still chooses every search and every list; the tools only do the mechanical part. That keeps them within rule 11, and since they identify controls by the model's references and by meaning, they should carry over to the private sites. The agent measures steps, time and tokens on 2 or 3 real reading tasks, with and without the tools, so we'll know what it saves before merging.

Eight agents are running now. I'll merge them one by one as they finish and report.

